// Lesson 01 effects — reveal, wipe, and mark acceptance.
//
// Runs AFTER ser-estar-lesson.script on slide 1 of "Animation Script test".
// It preserves the chalk-board scene and cell-by-cell content created by the
// base lesson and demonstrates one of each effect:
//
// - reveal on the conjugation table as a composite subtree (cell text is
//   ordinary renderable content; empty layout slots stay out),
// - wipe on one example translation sentence (a single text node holding the
//   full sentence),
// - mark on the lesson title as a temporary overlay.
//
// Timing sits inside the base lesson so seeks stay meaningful: the mark draws
// while the title is shown, the table reveal starts with the table fade, and
// the wipe runs after its example appears. The reveal carries an optional
// `sound:` SFX; the wipe and mark stay silent.
script "Lesson 01 effects" from 0
bind grid = table("Grammar table")
bind sentence = node("ex1t")
bind title = node("Lesson title")
bind sfx = audio("Scratch")
mark(title, at: 1, over: 1, visual: none)
reveal(grid, at: 5, over: 1, visual: none, sound: sfx)
wipe(sentence, at: 18, over: 1, visual: none)
